  "prompt": "Design the GEOSPATIAL MAP workspace screen for ClimateGuard AI.\nLayout:\n- Top Map Toolbar:\n  Layer toggles: Flood Inundation Layer, Heatwave Anomaly Layer, Drought Moisture Deficit, Satellite Imagery (NASA GIBS), Active Fire (FIRMS), Location Markers.\n  Controls: Coordinate Search (\"Lat / Long or City Name\"), Opacity Slider (80%), Map Projection toggle, Zoom In/Out, Measure Tool, Fullscreen.\n- Main Map Canvas (Full view with custom dark tactical cartography):\n  Detailed vector/satellite map visualization with glowing danger zones, river network vectors, heat contour gradients, and interactive risk pins.\n- Floating Right Tactical Telemetry Panel:\n  Selected Location: \"Indus Basin - Sector North-West (31.5204° N, 74.3587° E)\"\n  Live Telemetry: Temperature (39.4°C), Relative Humidity (72%), Rainfall (84mm / 24h), River Discharge (8,420 m³/s - Exceeds 95th Percentile).\n  Current Hazard Status: \"FLOOD ALERT LEVEL 3 - High Risk\" with countdown to peak flood surge (Est. 14h 20m).\n  Data Sources: \"Open-Meteo Flood API + NASA GIBS MODIS Surface Reflection\".\n  Action: \"Simulate Parametric Payout\" & \"Export GeoJSON Report\".\n- Bottom Map Legend:\n  Gradient scales for Flood severity (Low to Critical #EF4444), Surface Temp (°C), and Soil Moisture index. Real satellite timestamp \"Last sync: 6 mins ago via Sentinel-2 / GPM\".",
